[size=5]Triumvirate — Enderal Conversion[/size]

[i]Enai Siaion's five mage archetypes, rebuilt so Enderal can actually give you the spells, and so the Shaman stops praying to the All-Maker.[/i]
[line]
[size=4]Overview[/size]

Triumvirate adds [b]75 spells and 26 staves[/b] across five archetypes: Druid, Shadow Mage, Warlock, Cleric and Shaman. In Enderal, out of the box, it [b]loads perfectly and you can never obtain a single spell[/b]. There is no crash and no error. Its distribution script hands the tomes to Skyrim merchants and loot lists, and not one of them exists in Enderal.

This conversion is Triumvirate's own plugin, rebuilt for Enderal:

[list]
[*][b]Every spell has a home.[/b] Each spell line is sold by one named Enderal merchant, Novice to Master, plus its staves. The lines Enderal outlaws (Entropy and Psionics for the Sun Temple's archetypes) are hidden in the world instead, one copy each, with a letter explaining how they got there.[/*]
[*][b]The high tiers can actually appear.[/b] Vanilla gates Adept, Expert and Master tomes on skill globals that only a Skyrim quest ever lowers. Enderal does not have that quest, so 45 of the 75 tomes could never show up. The gate is removed.[/*]
[*][b]Enderal prices and mana costs.[/b] Tomes are repriced onto Enderal's 20–350 gold range, and every spell gets a written mana cost on Enderal's scale (the original Master tier cost up to 1,484 mana; Enderal's dearest spell is 310). Damage, durations and effects are untouched.[/*]
[*][b]Clean masters and no Skyrim leftovers.[/b] The three DLC masters (260 dead references), four injected Skyrim cells and an override of Enderal's prologue worldspace are all removed.[/*]
[*][b]Enderal's own scripts protected.[/b] Triumvirate's archive overwrites two of Enderal's deliberately emptied brawl scripts; Enderal's versions are shipped loose so they win again.[/*]
[*][b]Tamriel is gone from the text.[/b] Hircine, Azra, Oblivion and the All-Maker are renamed into Enderal's own vocabulary (listed per archetype below), and the five schools use Enderal's names.[/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=4]Requirements and install order[/size]

[list=1]
[*][b]Enderal: Forgotten Stories (Special Edition).[/b] Checked against version [b]2.1.4.4[/b].[/*]
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/39170]Triumvirate — Mage Archetypes by Enai Siaion[/url][/b], version [b]1.8.0[/b] exactly. Install it first and normally. Its two BSAs supply every mesh and texture. [b]This download contains none of them.[/b][/*]
[*][b]This mod, installed over it and allowed to OVERWRITE.[/b] It replaces [font=Courier New]Triumvirate - Mage Archetypes.esp[/font] with the converted plugin and adds three loose scripts under [font=Courier New]Scripts\[/font]. It must sit [b]below Triumvirate in MO2's left pane[/b] (file order).[/*]
[*]Keep [font=Courier New]Triumvirate - Mage Archetypes.esp[/font] [b]enabled[/b]. Do not rename it: the BSAs only load while a plugin of that exact name is active, which is why this is a replacement and not a patch.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Nothing else is needed:[/b] no SKSE plugin, no SkyUI/MCM, no PapyrusUtil. [b]Do not use it with any other Triumvirate version[/b]; it is a rebuild of 1.8.0's records.

[i]Merchant stock refreshes every two in-game days. On an existing save, give a shop 48 hours before judging what it carries.[/i]
[line]
[size=4]The archetypes[/size]

Tiers run [b]Novice → Apprentice → Adept → Expert → Master[/b]. Enderal renames the five schools: Alteration is [b]Mentalism[/b], Conjuration is [b]Entropy[/b], Destruction is [b]Elementalism[/b], Illusion is [b]Psionics[/b] and Restoration is [b]Light Magic[/b]. Spells marked [b]†[/b] were renamed for Enderal; the original name follows.

