[*]Shield of Awe's release sound never played (it was gated on a Skyrim civil-war global). Fixed.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Kept deliberately:[/b] Fylgja, Goodberry and Horned Lord are Norse and D&D loans, not Elder Scrolls terms. Elsewhere, "Draugr" and undead became [b]Lost Ones[/b], Oblivion as a place became [b]Sinistra[/b] or [b]the Sea of Eventualities[/b], and "Daedric" on internal summon records became "Demon".
[line]
[size=4]Compatibility and load order[/size]

This [b]is[/b] [font=Courier New]Triumvirate - Mage Archetypes.esp[/font]. It takes the original's place in your load order, where that plugin already sat. It is a full ESP, not ESL-flagged, because it carries all of Triumvirate's records.

[b]It overrides no merchant chest, no NPC and no faction belonging to Enderal.[/b] Beyond Triumvirate's own records it touches six:
[list]
[*][b]Four leveled lists that were empty.[/b] Enderal ships 67 [font=Courier New]<Merchant>_CustomMerchandise[/font] lists, one inside each merchant's chest and every one of them empty, an extension point SureAI never filled. Stock goes there, so the merchants' chests are never edited.[/*]
[*][b]One quest-reward chest[/b] (the Apothecarii stash), which no other mod touches.[/*]
[*][b]One interior cell[/b] (Yero's vault), only to place a chest of its own. No navmesh and no existing object is changed.[/*]
[/list]

[list]
[*][b]Enderal SE - Gameplay Overhaul (EGO)[/b] and [b]EGO SE - Leveling Redone:[/b] compatible in any order. They rewrite several of these merchants' chests and keep the lists this mod fills.[/*]
[*][b]KataPUMB Spell Package:[/b] compatible. It adds staves to Torius's and Tarhutie's chests directly.[/*]
[*][b]Apocalypse — Enderal Conversion:[/b] both mods stock [b]Torius Flameling[/b] and [b]Tarhutie[/b] through the same lists, so with both installed only the later-loading plugin's additions appear in those two shops. Load this mod after Apocalypse to keep Druid, Shaman, Cleric and Warlock Elementalism for sale; that costs Apocalypse its Apprentice and Expert tomes. Apocalypse's distribution is being reworked to move off both.[/*]
[*][b]Any other mod using the same lists:[/b] only the additions are at stake, never a merchant's whole inventory.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Pinned to Triumvirate 1.8.0.[/b] A newer Triumvirate must not be used with this until it is refreshed.
[line]
[size=4]Known limitations[/size]

[list]
[*][b]Force of Nature is withheld.[/b] On some setups it leaves the player invisible while transformed. That reproduces with a plain console race change and no mod scripts at all, so it is outside this mod. The spell is intact; it is simply not sold. Wildshape, the Druid's other transformation, works.[/*]
[*][b]The hidden Entropy and Psionics tomes are one copy each and do not restock.[/b] Read them before you sell them.[/*]
[*][b]Aurora Leklerk[/b] is part of the Forgotten Stories quest "Cuthbert's Legacy". Her shop has no quest condition on it, but whether she trades before that quest is done is not yet confirmed in game.[/*]
[*][b]The Druid's doubled summons never fire.[/b] Twin Souls, the vanilla perk that gates them, does not exist in Enderal, so the single-summon versions always fire.[/*]
[*][b]The Warlock's summons are always base strength.[/b] Same reason: Elemental Potency gates the [i]Potent[/i] variants. Enderal's Sinistrope line has no summoned-creature perk to stand in.[/*]
[*][b]The Shadow Mage's Possession never affects automatons[/b] (Starling constructs), because the Master of the Mind perk is absent. That is vanilla's behaviour for a player without the perk.[/*]
[*][b]Three Spirit Guardian variants are never chosen.[/b] Triumvirate ships one per race, including Argonian, Khajiit and Orc, which no Enderal player can be. Every Enderal race still gets a guardian.[/*]
[*][b]Tiers follow Enai's ranks[/b], not playtesting against Enderal's difficulty curve. Feedback welcome.[/*]
[*][b]Tome names carry no "(Rank N)" suffix.[/b] In Enderal that suffix means the same spell exists at another strength; Triumvirate's spells have one version each, like Enderal's 13 unsuffixed tomes.[/*]
[*][b]Non-English games[/b] show the two places this mod touches (the Apothecarii chest and Yero's vault) with English names, because the plugin is not localized.[/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=4]Credits[/size]

[b]Enai Siaion[/b] (with [b]Mihail[/b] for creature assets) — Triumvirate: all 75 spells, the five archetypes, every design decision and every asset. [b]This release is his plugin, modified.[/b] It exists so his work reaches you in a different game. Redistributed under the mod's stated permissions, which allow modification and re-upload with credit. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/39170]Go and endorse the original[/url]; you need it installed anyway.

[b]SureAI[/b] — Enderal: Forgotten Stories, the two brawl scripts shipped here verbatim, the 67 unused merchant lists that made the distribution conflict-free, and the lore every new name and both letters were drawn from.
[line]
